.sty files go in whatever directory you're running LaTeX in, or in a central folder LaTeX knows about.

**New!** I've changed bindery.sty so that it better handles different page sizes. It now decides whether 
page size is in the A series (common outside the United States) or US letter paper (common in the United 
States) by page height/width ratios rather than what class option is present, so it should handle wacky 
page sizes like A7 or whatever just fine.

I've replaced the old environment system (two environments, letter and a4) with a new eight-environment system. 
* LaTeX code in the *folio* environment will be included for both letter folio and A4 folio output.
* LaTeX code in the *quarto* environment will be included for both letter quarto and A4 quarto output.
* LaTeX code in the *iso* environment will be included for both A4 folio and A4 quarto output.
* LaTeX code in the *usletter* environment will be included for both letter folio and letter quarto output.
* LaTeX code in the *letterfolio* environment will be included for letter folio output only.
* LaTeX code in the *a4folio* environment will be included for A4 folio output only.
* LaTeX code in the *letterquarto* environment will be included for letter quarto output only.
* LaTeX code in the *a4quarto* environment will be included for A4 quarto output only.


I've placed a cleaned up scan of Rackham's drawing for the endpapers in images (images/endpaper.jpg), in case 
it's useful to someone.

Fonts used are:
* EB Garamond: https://www.1001freefonts.com/eb-garamond.font
* Menuetto https://www.1001freefonts.com/menuetto.font
* Acorn Initials https://www.1001freefonts.com/acorn.font
